# C6.30: git pathspecs that form the corresponding source of the shipped opendana
# binary (GPL-3.0-or-later): everything needed to build, install, run and modify
# it. packaging/make-sources.sh archives exactly these paths of the packaged
# commit with `git archive`, then removes any file the ROM auditor flags.
# Deliberately NOT included: docs/ (reports and reference captures), tests/ (fixtures
# derived from the original), mods/ and content/ (example levels copied from the
# original), tools/ (development and audit tooling). None is needed to build opendana;
# CMake disables the test runner when tests/ is absent.
CMakeLists.txt
build.sh
LICENSE
NOTICE
README.md
docs/MODDING.md
external
include
schema
src
assets/fonts
packaging
# C6.51: macOS is out of scope and its scripts name a private host, a VM and a
# person; they stay out of the corresponding source (the private lab keeps them).
:(exclude)packaging/build-macos.sh
:(exclude)packaging/macos-remote-build.sh
:(exclude)packaging/macos-sources.sha256
